insert into nodes (node_type, slug, title, summary, status, meta_title, meta_description, legacy_slugs, published_at) values ('article', 'underwater-hotels-and-restaurants-in-maldives', 'Underwater Hotels and Restaurants In Maldives', 'List of underwater hotels and restaurants in maldives.', 'published', 'Underwater Hotels and Restaurants In Maldives | Maldives Travel Guide | MTG', 'List of underwater hotels and restaurants in maldives.', ARRAY['/articles/underwater-hotel-in-maldives.html']::text[], now()) on conflict (node_type, slug) do nothing;
insert into articles (id, body, reading_time_minutes) select id, '<p>Maldives Underwater SPA Maldives Underwater Restaurants Ithaa M6M 5.8 SUBSIX SEA H2O Maldives Underwater Resort Rooms The Muraka The Aqua Villa FAQs</p><h2>Maldives Underwater Spa</h2><h3>PEARL Underwater Spa at Huvafen Fushi</h3><p>PEARL Underwater Spa is the first underwater Spa in the world</p><p>A mysterious underwater realm awaits you eight meters below the surface. Welcome to the world''s first and only underwater spa treatment rooms. Experiential opportunities that come along just once in a lifetime. Only available in Huvafen Fushi.</p><p>The currents in the ocean ebb and flow. The tides have an effect on your senses. Panoramic views of the reef and a calming design inspired by the sea''s colors and textures. Take in the soothing tranquility of a sanctuary below.</p><p>There are two underwater chambers in this underwater Wonder. Pearl Spa, in addition to being physically stunning, provides a wide range of classic and modern massages and holistic treatments.</p><p>Costs 285$</p><h2>Maldives Underwater Restaurants</h2><h3>ITHAA Underwater restaurant at Conrad Maldives Rangali Island</h3><p>Ithaa is the first underwater restaurant in the world</p><p>Dine five meters beneath the ocean''s surface at the world''s first undersea restaurant, which offers panoramic views of the coral garden and fusion cuisines paired with exquisite wines. Ithaa is available for private dinners, weddings, and other special events.</p><p>Local cuisines are combined with Western influences on the set lunch and dinner menus, which are paired with a wine idea. Mid-morning drinks are also available at our pioneering restaurant.</p><p>The tiny restaurant, whose name in the native Dhivehi language means &quot;mother-of-pearl,&quot; seats only 14 people and serves contemporary European food.</p><p>Costs around 240$</p><h3>M6m Underwater Restaurant at OZEN at Maadhoo</h3><p>Six meters beneath the Indian Ocean, exquisite fine dining with a degustation menu showcasing innovative modern seafood cuisine and great wine pairings. M6m (Minus Six Meters), the best underwater restaurant in the Maldives, is the crown gem of OZEN LIFE MAADHOO''s exquisite dining experiences.</p><p>Children are only admitted on select days so that adults may completely enjoy the romantic dinner experience at the underwater restaurant near Malé. In the meanwhile, while parents enjoy their M6m visit, children may participate in an interesting program at the kids'' club, which includes tasty food.</p><p>Begin with an amazing combination of Fine Caviar and Champagne in the stylish M6m Lounge above before heading downstairs for an unforgettable dining experience. You will be indulged with extremely Masterful Seafood Dishes and Perfect Wine Pairings while surrounded by a turquoise lagoon and the breath-taking Maldivian undersea environment.</p><p>Costs 190$ for inhouse guests</p><h3>5.8 Underwater Restaurant at Hurawalhi</h3><p>5.8 Undersea Restaurant is a byword for superb gourmet dining in the Maldives, combining an appealing setting beneath the sea with delicious meals. Diners who want to experience the world''s largest all-glass underwater restaurant will be astounded not just by the unique environment, but also by 5.8''s five-star meals.</p><p>The new lunch and evening menus combine high-quality, sustainably sourced foods with bold technique and presentation inventiveness. Light meals include tuna tartare and seared scallops with wasabi and avocado, as well as smoked langoustine with a trio of caviar and lemon pearls, poached lobster, seared Wagyu beef tenderloin, and melt-in-your-mouth mango cheesecake with coconut ice cream.</p><p>Take your evening date to the restaurant at sunset to enjoy a 7-course meal and be stunned by both the daytime and romantic nighttime atmospheres, or book a table at noon (now available in two 5-course sittings) to see the restaurant when the sun and fishlife are at their finest.</p><p>Costs around 225$</p><h3>SUBSIX Underwater Bar Restaurant &amp; Nightclub at niyama maldives</h3><div data-youtube-id="wm8kohwgJhI" data-video-title="restaurant subsix maldives underwater"></div><p>By speedboat, you can go to Subsix and descend a stunning three-tier stairway. Italian abstract chandeliers, like shimmering coral, brighten the fall. In the depths, sink into the soft anemone seats beneath the gentle waves of capiz shells hung from the ceiling beneath the swooping curves of the clam-inspired bar.</p><p>Enjoy Champagne brunches, subaquatic lunches, gourmet dinners, and adults-only glow parties all against the backdrop of the reef''s theater.</p><p>Costs 200$</p><h3>SEA Underwater Restaurant &amp; Wine Cellar at Anantara Kihavah</h3><p>An unique Maldivian dining experience awaits you beneath the waves. Before arriving to a dining area completely encircled by the sea, see the world''s first underwater wine cellar. As you savor gourmet meals at its finest, watch sharks, turtles, and tropical fish swim past.</p><p>You will not be disappointed when you visit Anantara Kihavah, a boutique hotel with all the benefits of a paradise island of dreams - white beaches with fringed palm trees, turquoise seas, devoted butlers, great cuisine, and luxury Over Water Villas. In fact, with an underwater wine cellar, six overwater spa rooms, and a 49-meter long infinity swimming pool, one of the longest in the Maldives, the reality will exceed any of your aspirations. The resort is located on Kihavah Huravalhi, one of the most pristine Maldivian Islands, and is accessible via a 30-minute seaplane flight from Velana International Airport, which is an unforgettable experience in and of itself as the plane flies over a string of glowing coral islands and Maldives resorts amid turquoise waters. There are 74 one-bedroom villas and four two-bedroom apartments in total.</p><p>Costs around 245$</p><h3>H2O Underwater Restaurant at YOU &amp; ME by Cocoon</h3><div data-youtube-id="GshhbowTAOY" data-video-title="h20 cocoon maldives underwater restaurant"></div><p>The standout feature of You &amp; Me by Cocoon is a fully submerged, underwater restaurant that offers customers a 360-degree view of the Maldives'' stunning marine environment while enjoying a delectable meal.</p><p>You &amp; Me by Cocoon Maldives, which debuted on February 1, 2019, is the newest premium &quot;adults only&quot; resort for honeymooners and couples in the Maldives. You &amp; Me by Cocoon, located on a private island in the northern Maldives'' Raa Atoll, offers a quiet, romantic refuge in exquisite, &quot;rustic-chic&quot; settings. The resort is one of the popular go-to sites for honeymooners, with spacious 109 Villas - 99 are over water and 10 are on the beach, six dining options serving world-class food in breathtaking surroundings, the over-water Orchid Spa, the enormous swimming pool, and water sports center. Look no farther if you''re searching for five-star quality and service in a lush environment of unrivaled tropical splendor.</p><p>Costs 190$</p><h2>Maldives Underwater Hotels</h2><h3>The MURAKA Underwater Residence At Conrad Maldives Rangali Island</h3><div data-youtube-id="9vs_dfZcijI" data-video-title="The MURAKA Underwater Villa maldives"></div><p>THE MURAKA is the first underwater hotel in the world</p><p>THE MURAKA, part of the Conrad Maldives Rangali Island resort, is a one-of-a-kind luxury two-story property with a master bedroom buried nearly 16 feet below sea level in the Indian Ocean.</p><p>Above water, you''ll find living and dining spaces worthy of one of the world''s most opulent homes.</p><p>There are two bedrooms and a bathroom with an ocean view tub.</p><p>Infinity pool on an outdoor deck.</p><p>Butler on call 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.</p><p>Make your way to your private underwater aquarium and architectural wonder via the spiral staircase or elevator.</p><p>The master bedroom features an acrylic dome that curves 180 degrees.</p><p>Bathroom with floor-to-ceiling windows and walk-in closet.</p><p>Theater dedicated to tunnel gazing.</p><p>To reserve a reservation at The Muraka, a 50% payment is needed at the time of booking, which is refundable up to 30 days prior to arrival. Bookings for the Muraka that occur between the 21st of December 2022 and the 9th of January 2023 will need a 100 percent deposit and can be cancelled 60 days prior to arrival without incurring a retention penalty.</p><p>Costs around 50,000$</p><h3>The AQUA Villa Underwater Bedroom At Pullman Maldives Maamutaa</h3><p>Discover Pullman''s The Aqua Villa experience, an immersive encounter with aquatic life from the luxury of your bed that will nourish and bring to life your childhood fantasies. Enjoy the peace and tranquility of the Indian Ocean while finding the ideal combination of play and refreshment.</p><p>Because Pullman is a firm believer in combining work and pleasure, there''s a lot more to do at Pullman Maldives than just kick back, sleep, and take a picture.</p><p>This luxurious two-storey Aqua Villa features a submerged master bedroom with an overwater bedroom, as well as plenty of space to relax and live your once-in-a-lifetime adventure.</p><p>The Aqua Villa Experience is the realization of your childhood fantasies. It''s a game, but not the one you''re used to. It''s the kind of thing you want to share with the rest of the world. And, more crucially, with your closest friends and family.</p><p>Consider the tranquility of diving without the use of a tank. Or swapping midnight secrets in your own personal aquarium. You can''t possibly be serious? We thrive on the impossible at Pullman.</p><p>Prepare to explore the charm of the ocean while enjoying the elegant luxury that we have to offer, with one submerged bedroom beneath the turquoise waves. In the Maldives, the Aqua Villas are a rarity, and Pullman is delighted to be a pioneer in immersive travel for this area.</p><p>Costs around 650$</p><h4>Questions and Answers</h4><p>The underwater hotel room in the Pullman Maldives cost around 650$ per night</p><p>And it''s not beach eating anymore; instead, there are five magnificent underwater restaurants in the Maldives that you must visit if you want to make your stay on the island a memorable one. To make this a night to remember, book a reservation at one of these restaurants with your significant other.</p><p>According to various NASA and USGS estimates, about 80% of the Maldives might become uninhabitable by 2050 if global warming continues at its current rate. &quot;Our islands are gradually being swamped by the water, one by one,&quot; Maldives President Ibrahim Mohamed Solih told the United Nations.</p><p>Before taxes, the Muraka costs $50,000 each night. However, this price includes a three-bedroom villa with two bathrooms, a kitchen, living room, dining area, and an infinity pool on the terrace.</p>', 8 from nodes where node_type = 'article' and slug = 'underwater-hotels-and-restaurants-in-maldives' on conflict (id) do nothing;
